xamined. We study the capabilities of computer technology with DNA analysis.<\/jats:p>","container-title":["Bulletin of Science and Practice"],"is-referenced-by-count":1},{"DOI":"10.21519\/0234-2758-2020-36-2-43-55","title":["Antitumor Activity of Indole-3-carbinol in Breast Cancer Cells: Phenotype, Genetic Pattern, DNA Methylation Inversion"],"issued":{"date-parts":[[2020]]},"author":[{"given":"E.L.","family":"Muyzhnek","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Russian Scientific Center of Roentgenology and Radiology, Moscow, 117997 Russia"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"S.V.","family":"Nikulin","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Bioclinicum Scientific Research Center, Moscow, 115088 Russia"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"A.D.","family":"Kaprin","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"P.A. Hertzen Moscow Oncology Research Center, National Medical Research Radiological Center, Moscow, 125284 Russia"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"L.A.","family":"Ashrafyan","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"National Medical Research Center for Obstetrics, Gynecology and Perinatology named after Academician V.I. Kulakov, Moscow, 117997 Russia"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"N.I.","family":"Rozhkova","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"P.A. Hertzen Moscow Oncology Research Center, National Medical Research Radiological Center, Moscow, 125284 Russia"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"P.G.","family":"Labazanova","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"P.A. Hertzen Moscow Oncology Research Center, National Medical Research Radiological Center, Moscow, 125284 Russia"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"V.I.","family":"Kiselev","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"National Medical Research Center for Obstetrics, Gynecology and Perinatology named after Academician V.I. Kulakov, Moscow, 117997 Russia"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"abstract":"<jats:p>The effect of indole-3-carbinol on a number of functions and characteristics of MDA-MB-231 breast cancer cells and MCF-10A healthy breast tissue cells has been studied. It was shown that indole-3-carbinol significantly reduced the proliferation and migration of MDA-MB-231 cells and does not affect these functions in MCF-10A cells. Incubation of MDA-MB-231 tumor cells with indole-3-carbinol (100 uM) for 48 h resulted in a marked decrease in the expression of the Wnt cascade genes, CCND1 (by 28%), SP1 (by 44%), CDK6 (by 47%), as well as EGFR (by 64%) and FASN (by 22%) genes. Incubation of MCF-10A cell line under the same conditions induced a noticeable decrease in expression of only two genes, EGFR (by 16%) and CDK6 (by 9%). In addition, indole-3-carbinol was also shown to manifest a selective DNA demethylation activity in breast tumor cells and to reverse the process of abnormal methylation and functional blockage of the anti-tumor WIF1 gene. These data indicate that drags containing indole-3-carbinol as an active component can be potential regulators of epigenetic processes in the treatment of breast cancer and other tumors.\n\nindole-3-carbinol, breast cancer, epigenetics, Wnt<\/jats:p>","container-title":["Biotekhnologiya"],"is-referenced-by-count":0}],"items-per-page":50,"query":{"start-index":0,"search-terms":"\u0441\u0432\u0435\u0436\u0438\u0435 \u0437\u0435\u0440\u043a\u0430\u043b\u044c\u043d\u044b\u0435 \u0446\u0435\u043f\u043e\u0447\u043a\u0438 \u0414\u041d\u041a"}}}